WEB SOURCE (THE SPEC)
  components/ai/AIQuietHoursSuggestion.tsx — `withAiFeature('quiet-hours-suggestion', InnerSection)`
  drives `useAiStream({ url:'/ai/settings/quiet-hours/draft', body:{}, onEvent: handleEvent })` and
  renders `AIFeatureCard` (title + cyan Helix badge + description + universal "Ask Helix" action,
  buttonPlacement="below", NO inputSlot) with `children` = the captured-proposal block (an "Apply to
  form" primary button + a reviewable window preview), then the streamed `AiOutputPanel`. The panel
  takes NO vehicleId and NO prompt — its only POST field is the empty object, so the button gate is
  purely `canStart = stream.state !== 'paused-confirm'`. `handleEvent` captures a typed proposal from a
  `tool_result` whose `name === 'draft_quiet_hours_window' && ev.ok`, validating start_local/end_local/
  timezone (string), weekdays (number), bypass_severities (array); it FILTERS bypass_severities to its
  string elements, defaults status→'ok' and existing_windows_count→0. "Apply to form" forwards
  `{enabled:true, start_local, end_local, timezone, weekdays, bypass_severities}` to the parent
  `onApplyDraft` (the baseline QuietHoursPanel Save button stays the sole write path — ADR-015 §I3+§I8).
  The unmount effect runs `cancelStream()` AND `setProposal(null)`.

